From 5bbb06bf434ae5f91a9275b4b9c0e8bceaa5e8fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:33:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer, windowing/gbm: Dolby Vision measured from the
 HDR10 picture, for the video that plays

Some old Blu-ray discs carry a Dolby Vision grade whose metadata are flat; for those, a user
prefers what "HDR10 as Dolby Vision, measured" makes of the HDR10 picture, but the TV takes the
RPU of the file, and the only way round was to strip Dolby Vision from the file (issue #6,
2026-10-26).

"Dolby Vision output (this video)", in the video settings of the player, gets a value "Dolby
Vision measured from the HDR10 picture" (DVBRIDGE::OutputChoice::MEASURED). It is offered only
where the base layer is the HDR10 version of the film (profile 7 with base layer compatibility
6, and 8.1: BaseLayerIsHdr10()), where the stream's Dolby Vision is its own (not made from its
HDR10+ metadata nor measured already), and where native output can be had. Chosen, the video
stream is opened again, as with the other values, and its decoder leaves the stream's RPU and
its enhancement layer aside (no FEL decoding: NeedsDVEnhancement()) and gives each picture the
placeholder metadata of HDR10 measured as Dolby Vision (MakeMeasuredMetadata()); the window
system then measures the pictures as it does for HDR10. Nothing changes by default, nor for any
other value or video; like the other values it is for that video only (Kodi keeps the settings
of a file in fixed columns of its video database, and a column of Hades' own would change its
schema under a version number that Kodi will use for something else).

Fail-closed: where the HDR10 does not say the luminance of its mastering display there are no
measured metadata, and the pictures go to the ordinary output as the HDR10 base layer, said once
in the log; where native output cannot be had, the base layer plays as Kodi plays it (never
reconstructed as HDR10: ConversionSettingFor()). The page "Dolby Vision" of the player
information says that the metadata are measured (hades.dv.origin), and the log says the choice
and what the decoder does with it.

Tested on the host: the rules of DVPlaybackPolicy.h (23 checks, four mutations caught), and the
earlier policy test of the choices (112 checks) against the new header. String in English,
translated in Estuary (es_es, es_ar, es_mx).
